.TH PODLAB 1 "" "podlab" "podlab manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
podlab \- The classes of hostile hosts as profiles: list them, check one
against this host, or run a command in a lab of one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpodlab COMMAND [OPTIONS]\fR
.PP
\fBStart here:\fR
.TP
\fBpodlab list\fR
List each profile.
.TP
\fBpodlab check PROFILE\fR
Check a profile on this host.
.TP
\fBpodlab man\fR
Read the manual.
.PP
\fBRead the profiles:\fR
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List each profile, its parts, and what holds each part in a lab
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Check a profile on this host with the probes of pod\-hostprobe, or against a
JSON report of pod\-hostprobe
.PP
\fBRun in a lab:\fR
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Run a command in a lab of a profile. The lab checks itself before the command;
a part that does not hold stops the run
.PP
\fBRead the manual:\fR
.TP
\fBman\fR
The manual: each command, profile, variable and exit code. A pager shows it on
a terminal
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help.
.SH DESCRIPTION
podlab holds the classes of hostile hosts as profiles. A profile names the
probe rows that each part refuses or allows.
.PP
podlab check compares a profile with this host, or with a JSON report of
pod\-hostprobe. A part holds, fails, or cannot be observed here.
.PP
podlab run runs a command in a lab of a profile. The lab holds each part with
no root: a seccomp filter, Landlock, mounts in a user namespace, a network
namespace and inherited descriptors.
.PP
The lab measures the profile from inside before the command. A part that does
not hold stops the run, unless \-\-partial is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "podlab list"
List each profile, its parts, and what holds each part in a lab.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodlab list [OPTIONS]\fR
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
List each profile and its parts.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab list
.fi
.RE
.SS "podlab check"
Check a profile on this host with the probes of pod\-hostprobe, or against a
JSON report of pod\-hostprobe.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodlab check [OPTIONS] PROFILE\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIPROFILE\fR
The name of the profile.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR \fIFILE\fR
A JSON report of pod\-hostprobe to check, in place of the probes of this host.
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR \fINAME:PORT\fR
Run the rows that send a packet past this host, to this name and port. The
probes use the proxy of HTTPS_PROXY. With no value, these rows do not run.
.TP
\fB\-\-network\-other\fR \fINAME\fR
A second name for the rows that send a packet out.
.TP
\fB\-\-network\-literal\fR \fIADDRESS\fR
An IP address for the rows that send a packet out.
.TP
\fB\-\-network\-closed\fR \fIPORT\fR
The port that the proxy refuses or holds with no byte. Default: 22.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
\-\-network\-other needs \-\-network.
.PP
\-\-network\-literal needs \-\-network.
.PP
\-\-network\-closed needs \-\-network.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Check the profile userns\-off on this host.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab check userns\-off
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check a profile against a report of pod\-hostprobe.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab check bind\-denied \-\-report report.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "podlab run"
Run a command in a lab of a profile. The lab checks itself before the command;
a part that does not hold stops the run.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodlab run [OPTIONS] PROFILE CMD...\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIPROFILE\fR
The name of the profile.
.TP
\fICMD...\fR
The command and its arguments.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-partial\fR
Run the command in the parts that hold, and report the others.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-connect\fR \fIPORT\fR
Let a TCP connect reach this port where the profile refuses each TCP connect
(the proxy of the host). Give it once for each port.
.TP
\fB\-\-way\-out\fR
Give a network lab a way out. The stand\-in proxy applies the rules of its
class. Then it sends a CONNECT to a name outside the lab to the real network.
It goes directly, or through the proxy of HTTPS_PROXY of this host. The
command never gets that proxy or its credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-serve\fR \fIPORT\fR
After the rules of the class, send a CONNECT to a name of the lab at this port
to the command on 127.0.0.1. In a class with a list of TLS names, a
ClientHello with a listed name goes to the first such port. Give it once for
each port.
.TP
\fB\-\-serve\-ca\fR \fIFILE\fR
A PEM file of the roots that check the TLS server of the command, where the
proxy of the class terminates TLS for the name. With no file, such a CONNECT
gets 502.
.TP
\fB\-\-expect\-exit\fR \fICODE\fR
The exit code that the command must give: a row of a failure. Another code
gives exit 4. A signal N is 128 + N.
.TP
\fB\-\-expect\-stderr\fR \fITEXT\fR
A text that the error output of the command must hold. The error output still
comes to this error output. Its absence gives exit 4.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
\-\-serve\-ca needs \-\-serve.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Run a command in a lab with a small /tmp.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run small\-tmp \-\- sh \-c 'df /tmp'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a command in a lab with no pseudo terminal.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run no\-ptmx \-\- sh \-c 'ls /dev'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a command in the parts that hold, and name the others.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run \-\-partial nonroot\-nocaps \-\- id
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a server in a network lab. Its clients reach it through the stand\-in
proxy with the rules of the class.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run \-\-serve 8443 proxy\-only \-\- ./server \-\-listen 127.0.0.1:8443
.fi
.RE
.SS "podlab man"
The manual: each command, profile, variable and exit code. A pager shows it on
a terminal.
.PP
Usage: \fBpodlab man [OPTIONS] [SECTION]...\fR
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fI[SECTION]...\fR
One section: a command, a topic, a table of facts.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Write the text with no pager, also on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-roff\fR
Write the manual as a man(7) page.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Write the manual as one JSON object.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the help of this command.
.PP
\fBRules:\fR
.PP
Give only one of \-\-json, \-\-roff.
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
Write the section of podlab check, with no pager.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab man \-\-no\-pager check
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
\fBThe lab:\fR
.TP
\fBTMPDIR\fR
The lab writes the files of the ids there. It is /tmp for the command, where a
part puts a tmpfs on /tmp. Used by: run. podlab reads it and sets it.
.TP
\fBHOME\fR
The directory that noexec\-home binds with noexec. Used by: run.
.PP
\fBA network lab:\fR
.TP
\fBHTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBhttps_proxy\fR, \fBHTTP_PROXY\fR, \fBhttp_proxy\fR
The stand\-in proxy of the lab, where the class has one. Else the lab removes
them. Used by: run. podlab sets it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBALL_PROXY\fR, \fBall_proxy\fR, \fBNO_PROXY\fR, \fBno_proxy\fR
The lab removes them: the command reaches out only as the class lets it. Used
by: run. podlab sets it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBGLOBAL_AGENT_HTTP_PROXY\fR, \fBGLOBAL_AGENT_HTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBnpm_config_proxy\fR, \fBnpm_config_https_proxy\fR, \fBNPM_CONFIG_PROXY\fR, \fBNPM_CONFIG_HTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBYARN_HTTP_PROXY\fR, \fBYARN_HTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBDOCKER_HTTP_PROXY\fR, \fBDOCKER_HTTPS_PROXY\fR
The proxy of a tool other than curl. The lab sets them to its stand\-in proxy
where the class has one. Else the lab removes them. Used by: run. podlab sets
it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBGLOBAL_AGENT_NO_PROXY\fR, \fBnpm_config_noproxy\fR, \fBNPM_CONFIG_NOPROXY\fR, \fBDOCKER_NO_PROXY\fR
The lab removes them. Used by: run. podlab sets it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_TYPE\fR, \fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_ADDRESS\fR, \fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_PORT\fR, \fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_USERNAME\fR, \fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_PASSWORD\fR, \fBCLOUDSDK_PROXY_RDNS\fR
The proxy of the Google Cloud CLI. The lab sets the type, the address, the
port and the credential of its stand\-in proxy where the class has one. Else
the lab removes them. Used by: run. podlab sets it and does not read it.
.TP
\fBJAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS\fR, \fBJDK_JAVA_OPTIONS\fR, \fB_JAVA_OPTIONS\fR
The options of a Java virtual machine. The lab removes each option of a proxy
from them, and keeps the other options. Used by: run. podlab reads it and sets
it.
.TP
\fBSSL_CERT_FILE\fR
The certificate file of the lab: the CA of the stand\-in servers, and the CA
of the proxy where the proxy terminates TLS. Used by: run. podlab sets it and
does not read it.
.PP
\fBThe pager:\fR
.TP
\fBPAGER\fR
The pager of the manual on a terminal. An empty value or cat writes the text
with no pager. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBTERM\fR
With no PAGER, less is used only when TERM names a terminal that is not dumb.
Used by: man.
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
The directories where the probe looks for less. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLINES\fR
The lines of a screen of the built\-in pager, when the terminal size is not
known. Used by: man.
.TP
\fBLESS\fR
The options of less. When it is not set, the pager sets FRX. Used by: man.
podlab reads it and sets it.
.SH "PROFILES"
Each profile, its parts, and what holds each part in a lab. podlab list prints
the same table.
.TP
\fBuserns\-off\fR
About: no user namespace for the caller. Parts: userns\-refused. Held by:
userns\-refused: seccomp: unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER), clone(CLONE_NEWUSER),
clone3. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBbind\-denied\fR
About: TCP bind and connect of AF_INET and AF_INET6 give EACCES; AF_UNIX
holds. Parts: tcp\-bind\-refused, tcp\-connect\-refused, unix\-allowed. Held
by: tcp\-bind\-refused: Landlock: no TCP port; tcp\-connect\-refused:
Landlock: no TCP port; unix\-allowed: the host. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBgetsockname\-denied\fR
About: getsockname gives EOPNOTSUPP. Parts: getsockname\-refused. Held by:
getsockname\-refused: seccomp: getsockname. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBproxy\-only\fR
About: no direct connection out; only an HTTP proxy with a credential reaches
out; no UDP. Parts: direct\-refused, proxy\-variable, proxy\-reaches,
proxy\-credential, port\-refused, udp\-refused. Held by: direct\-refused: a
network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128 with
a credential; proxy\-variable: a network namespace with no route out, a
stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128 with a credential; proxy\-reaches: a network
namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128 with a
credential; proxy\-credential: a network namespace with no route out, a
stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128 with a credential; port\-refused: a network
namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128 with a
credential; udp\-refused: seccomp: socket(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM),
socket(AF_INET6, SOCK_DGRAM), io_uring_setup. Source: podrunner, podssh,
podnet.
.TP
\fBsmall\-tmp\fR
About: TMPDIR on a tmpfs of 1 GiB. Parts: tmpdir\-small. Held by:
tmpdir\-small: tmpfs of 1073741824 bytes on /tmp. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBroot\-unreadable\fR
About: readdir("/") gives EACCES; an open by name holds. Parts:
root\-list\-refused, open\-by\-name. Held by: root\-list\-refused: Landlock: /
hidden; open\-by\-name: the host. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBnonroot\-nocaps\fR
About: a user that is not root, no capability, NoNewPrivs and a seccomp
filter. Parts: not\-root, no\-caps, no\-new\-privs, seccomp\-filter. Held by:
not\-root: the caller is not root; no\-caps: the caller is not root;
no\-new\-privs: no_new_privs; seccomp\-filter: seccomp: the default deny list
of pod\-confine. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBno\-kvm\fR
About: no /dev/kvm. Parts: kvm\-absent. Held by: kvm\-absent: Landlock:
/dev/kvm hidden. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBarm64\-tcg\fR
About: an arm64 host with no KVM: each guest runs on TCG. Parts: arm64,
kvm\-absent. Held by: arm64: not here: the machine tier of podvm; kvm\-absent:
Landlock: /dev/kvm hidden. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBinherited\-fds\fR
About: descriptors 3 to 9 open at the start. Parts: fds\-open. Held by:
fds\-open: descriptors 3 to 9. Source: podrunner.
.TP
\fBchroot\-denied\fR
About: chroot gives EPERM. Parts: chroot\-refused. Held by: chroot\-refused:
seccomp: chroot. Source: podvm.
.TP
\fBuserns\-mount\-denied\fR
About: a user namespace is made, and a mount in it fails
(apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns). Parts: userns\-made,
userns\-mount\-refused. Held by: userns\-made: the host;
userns\-mount\-refused: seccomp: mount, fsopen, fsmount, move_mount,
open_tree. Source: podvm.
.TP
\fBcgroup\-v1\fR
About: the cgroup v1 hierarchy, no cgroup2. Parts: cgroup\-v1. Held by:
cgroup\-v1: not here: the machine tier of podvm. Source: podvm.
.TP
\fBlandlock\-old\fR
About: a Landlock ABI below 4 (no TCP rules); a lab gives the form with no
Landlock. Parts: landlock\-below\-4. Held by: landlock\-below\-4: seccomp:
landlock_create_ruleset, landlock_add_rule, landlock_restrict_self. Source:
podvm.
.TP
\fBproc\-masked\fR
About: no /proc; no row measures the form with hidepid. Parts: proc\-hidden.
Held by: proc\-hidden: Landlock: /proc hidden. Source: podvm.
.TP
\fBnoexec\-tmp\fR
About: /tmp is mounted noexec. Parts: tmp\-noexec. Held by: tmp\-noexec: tmpfs
on /tmp, noexec. Source: podvm.
.TP
\fBlisten\-denied\fR
About: bind passes, and listen gives EACCES. Parts: bind\-allowed,
listen\-refused. Held by: bind\-allowed: the host; listen\-refused: seccomp:
listen. Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBudp\-denied\fR
About: no UDP: a UDP socket gives EPERM. Parts: udp\-refused. Held by:
udp\-refused: seccomp: socket(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM), socket(AF_INET6,
SOCK_DGRAM), io_uring_setup. Source: podnet, podssh.
.TP
\fBraw\-denied\fR
About: raw and packet sockets give EPERM. Parts: raw\-refused. Held by:
raw\-refused: seccomp: socket(AF_INET, SOCK_RAW), socket(AF_INET6, SOCK_RAW),
socket(AF_PACKET), io_uring_setup. Source: podnet.
.TP
\fBno\-ptmx\fR
About: no /dev/ptmx, no /dev/pts, and no controlling terminal. Parts:
ptmx\-absent, no\-ctty, tty\-opens. Held by: ptmx\-absent: a tmpfs on /dev
with no ptmx and no pts, a FIFO at /dev/tty; no\-ctty: a new session with no
controlling terminal; tty\-opens: a tmpfs on /dev with no ptmx and no pts, a
FIFO at /dev/tty. Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBno\-passwd\-entry\fR
About: the uid has no line in /etc/passwd, the gid none in /etc/group. Parts:
no\-id\-lines. Held by: no\-id\-lines: /etc/passwd and /etc/group with no line
of the caller. Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBnoexec\-home\fR
About: HOME is writable and noexec; /tmp runs programs. Parts: home\-noexec,
tmp\-exec. Held by: home\-noexec: HOME bound noexec; tmp\-exec: the host.
Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBno\-proc\fR
About: no /proc. Parts: proc\-absent. Held by: proc\-absent: an empty tmpfs on
/proc. Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBseccomp\-nonewprivs\fR
About: NoNewPrivs, no capability, and unshare, mount, chroot and ptrace
refused. Parts: no\-new\-privs, no\-caps, calls\-refused. Held by:
no\-new\-privs: no_new_privs; no\-caps: no capability, no_new_privs;
calls\-refused: seccomp: unshare, clone, clone3, setns, mount, umount2,
pivot_root, fsopen, fsmount, move_mount, open_tree, chroot, ptrace. Source:
podssh.
.TP
\fBno\-tun\fR
About: no /dev/net/tun. Parts: tun\-absent. Held by: tun\-absent: Landlock:
/dev/net/tun hidden. Source: podssh, podnet.
.TP
\fBno\-net\-admin\fR
About: no CAP_NET_ADMIN and no /dev/net/tun. Parts: no\-net\-admin,
tun\-absent. Held by: no\-net\-admin: no capability, no_new_privs;
tun\-absent: Landlock: /dev/net/tun hidden. Source: podnet.
.TP
\fBro\-etc\-ssl\fR
About: /etc/ssl is read\-only. Parts: etc\-ssl\-read\-only. Held by:
etc\-ssl\-read\-only: /etc/ssl bound read\-only. Source: podssh.
.TP
\fBno\-loopback\fR
About: no address on the loopback; AF_UNIX holds. Parts: loopback\-absent,
unix\-allowed. Held by: loopback\-absent: a network namespace with no
loopback; unix\-allowed: the host. Source: podnet.
.TP
\fBproxy\-tls\-reterminate\fR
About: the proxy shows its own CA for some names. Parts: proxy\-variable,
cert\-file, tls\-reterminated, ssh\-port\-silent. Held by: proxy\-variable: a
network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128;
cert\-file: a network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on
127.0.0.1:3128; tls\-reterminated: a network namespace with no route out, a
stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128; ssh\-port\-silent: a network namespace with
no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128. Source: podssh, podnet.
.TP
\fBproxy\-per\-name\fR
About: the proxy answers each name in its own way. Parts: proxy\-variable,
answer\-per\-name. Held by: proxy\-variable: a network namespace with no route
out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128; answer\-per\-name: a network
namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128. Source:
podssh, podnet.
.TP
\fBsni\-allowlist\fR
About: no proxy; TLS is reset for a name not on the list. Parts: no\-proxy,
sni\-reset. Held by: no\-proxy: a network namespace with no route out, a
stand\-in server on each IPv4 address, a filter of the TLS server name;
sni\-reset: a network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in server on each
IPv4 address, a filter of the TLS server name. Source: podssh, podnet.
.TP
\fBno\-proxy\-no\-dns\fR
About: no proxy and no resolver; only IP literals connect. Parts: no\-proxy,
no\-resolver, literal\-reaches. Held by: no\-proxy: a network namespace with
no route out, a stand\-in server on 192.0.2.0/24, no name server;
no\-resolver: a network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in server on
192.0.2.0/24, no name server; literal\-reaches: a network namespace with no
route out, a stand\-in server on 192.0.2.0/24, no name server. Source: podssh,
podnet.
.TP
\fBws\-upgrade\-refused\fR
About: the proxy refuses the WebSocket upgrade. Parts: proxy\-variable,
upgrade\-refused. Held by: proxy\-variable: a network namespace with no route
out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128; upgrade\-refused: a network
namespace with no route out, a stand\-in proxy on 127.0.0.1:3128. Source:
podssh, podnet.
.TP
\fBipv6\-only\fR
About: no IPv4 route; IPv6 reaches out. Parts: no\-ipv4\-route, ipv6\-reaches.
Held by: no\-ipv4\-route: a network namespace with no route out, a stand\-in
server on an IPv6 address, an IPv6 default route; ipv6\-reaches: a network
namespace with no route out, a stand\-in server on an IPv6 address, an IPv6
default route. Source: podnet.
.TP
\fBbind\-netns\-vm\-denied\fR
About: no TCP bind, a connect passes; no network namespace; process_vm_writev
refused; AF_UNIX holds. Parts: tcp\-bind\-refused, netns\-refused,
vm\-write\-refused, unix\-allowed. Held by: tcp\-bind\-refused: Landlock: no
TCP bind; netns\-refused: seccomp: unshare(CLONE_NEWNET), clone(CLONE_NEWNET),
clone3; vm\-write\-refused: seccomp: process_vm_writev; unix\-allowed: the
host. Source: podnet.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR (holds)
check: each part holds. run: the command exited 0, or it ended as
\-\-expect\-exit and \-\-expect\-stderr say.
.TP
\fB1\fR (fails)
check: a part does not hold.
.TP
\fB2\fR (usage)
A usage error of the command line.
.TP
\fB3\fR (unseen)
check: no part fails, and a part cannot be observed here.
.TP
\fB4\fR (unexpected)
run: the command ended in a way that \-\-expect\-exit or \-\-expect\-stderr
does not allow.
.TP
\fB125\fR (refused)
run: a part of the lab does not hold. The command did not run.
.TP
\fB126\fR (cannot\-exec)
run: the command did not start.
.TP
\fB127\fR (not\-found)
run: the command was not found.
.TP
\fB128+N\fR (signal)
run: the command ended on signal N.
.TP
\fBN\fR (command)
run: the exit code of the command, with no \-\-expect\-exit or
\-\-expect\-stderr. Each code that no other row names.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
List each profile and its parts.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check the profile userns\-off on this host.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab check userns\-off
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check a profile against a report of pod\-hostprobe.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab check bind\-denied \-\-report report.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a command in a lab with a small /tmp.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run small\-tmp \-\- sh \-c 'df /tmp'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a command in a lab with no pseudo terminal.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run no\-ptmx \-\- sh \-c 'ls /dev'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a command in the parts that hold, and name the others.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run \-\-partial nonroot\-nocaps \-\- id
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a server in a network lab. Its clients reach it through the stand\-in
proxy with the rules of the class.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab run \-\-serve 8443 proxy\-only \-\- ./server \-\-listen 127.0.0.1:8443
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write the section of podlab check, with no pager.
.RS 4
.nf
$ podlab man \-\-no\-pager check
.fi
.RE
